  <item>
      <name>Remap Caps Lock to Hyper</name>
      <appendix>OS X doesn't have a Hyper key, this snippet maps the caps lock (F19) to simulate pressing Control, Shift, Option and Command.  The rest of the mappings for it are configured in Keyboard Maestro.</appendix>
      <appendix> * Map Caps to Delete, when pressed by itself.</appendix>
      <appendix> * Map Scroll Lock to Caps Lock.</appendix>
 
      <identifier>caps_lock_to_hyper</identifier>

<!--
This sounded like a cool option but it does not do all the mappings correctly
      <autogen>__KeyOverlaidModifier__ 
		 KeyCode::F19,
	  KeyCode::VK_MODIFIER_MY_HYPER,
		 KeyCode::DELETE
      </autogen>
-->

        <!-- Caps is remapped to F19 in Seil, so here we map it to a crazy modifier combo and 
             also to delete when pressed by itself.
             -->
      <autogen>
	  __KeyOverlaidModifier__ 
      KeyCode::F19,

      KeyCode::COMMAND_L,
      ModifierFlag::OPTION_L | ModifierFlag::SHIFT_L | ModifierFlag::CONTROL_L,
	  KeyCode::DELETE
      </autogen>

	<autogen>
		__KeyToKey__
		KeyCode::PC_SCROLLLOCK,
		KeyCode::CAPSLOCK
	</autogen>

  </item>

  <item>
      <name>Custom mappings for control key</name>
      <appendix> * Map Command to Command+F2, when pressed by itself.</appendix>
      <appendix> * Map Command to Control, and Control to Command</appendix>
      <identifier>custom_mappings_control</identifier>
      <not>VI, TERMINAL</not>
      
      <!-- map command to command+F2 when pressed by itself, which allows it to be used to 
         start the launcher -->
      <autogen>
        __KeyOverlaidModifier__
        KeyCode::COMMAND_L,
        KeyCode::CONTROL_L,
        KeyCode::F2, ModifierFlag::COMMAND_L
      </autogen>

      <autogen>
          __KeyOverlaidModifier__
          KeyCode::CONTROL_L,
          KeyCode::COMMAND_L,
          KeyCode::F3, ModifierFlag::COMMAND_L
      </autogen>
  </item>

  <item>
      <name>Custom mappings for control key, without mapping to command</name>
      <identifier>custom_mappings_control_noremaptocommand</identifier>
      <only>VI, TERMINAL</only>
      <!-- map command to command+F2 when pressed by itself, which allows it to be used to 
         start the launcher -->
      <autogen>
        __KeyOverlaidModifier__
        KeyCode::COMMAND_L,
        KeyCode::COMMAND_L,
        KeyCode::F2, ModifierFlag::COMMAND_L
      </autogen>

      <autogen>
          __KeyOverlaidModifier__
          KeyCode::CONTROL_L,
          KeyCode::CONTROL_L,
          KeyCode::F3, ModifierFlag::COMMAND_L
      </autogen>
  </item>

</root>
